//? Title: Floyd–Steinberg dithering: actual diffusion, finite edges and tone
//? Subtitle: Preserve the original gradient, inspect native floating-point updates and measure the error that leaves the image
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A binary image can suggest intermediate brightness by varying the density of white
pixels. Floyd–Steinberg error diffusion quantizes pixels in raster order and transfers
the resulting errors to future neighbors. This report preserves the original forty-by-
sixty-four gradient and all its output pixels, inspects actual native updates, and
compares a threshold baseline with diffusion. Image edges discard weighted error, so
finite images do not have a guarantee of exact global or local tone preservation.
Work counts, floating-point evidence and input/quota controls make those limits explicit.
)

\toc

> The implemented raster rule

Scan each row left to right, from the top row down. At a pixel, the working value
already includes earlier diffusion. Values strictly below 128 become zero; values
at or above 128 become 255. Set e to working value minus that output and update the
future neighbors in this order: right by 7e/16, down-left by 3e/16, down by 5e/16,
and down-right by e/16. Skip neighbors outside the image, without renormalizing.

The fixed128 convention and traditional stencil are described in section3 of
[Speigle and Feng's research paper](https://corporate.jp.sharp/rd/journal-76/pdf/76-05.pdf).
Their later threshold-modulation and color extensions are outside this implementation.
The historical reference is R.W.Floyd and L.Steinberg, “An Adaptive Algorithm for
Spatial Greyscale,” Proceedings of the Society for Information Display17(2),75–77(1976).

The cutoff is part of the existing library contract. For an arbitrary double, 127.75
is closer to 255 than to zero, yet this implementation outputs zero for a single
pixel of that value. Describing it as unrestricted nearest-level rounding would be
incorrect. Working values are not clipped to0..255; feedback can push them beyond
that nominal grayscale range.

> Read the first diffusion and all four quantizations

A two-by-two image of128 provides a small exact example. The first output is255,
so e=-127. Its down-left neighbor is outside, discarding3e/16=-23.8125 at that step.
The following method diagram reads the native stencil and actual update records.
The table follows every actual raster quantization, including incoming errors.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_steinberg_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/grayscale_images.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_trace({{128.,128.},{128.,128.}});
  std::print("| row | column | actual working value | output | error | discarded numerator /16 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto&r:t.steps)std::print("| {} | {} | {:.12g} | {} | {:.12g} | {} |\n",r.row,r.col,r.value_before,r.quantized,r.error,r.discarded_numerator);
  const auto&w=t.work;std::print("\nTiny totals: input {}; output {}; white {}; actual updates {}; discarded slots {}; boundary loss {}; balance residual {}.\n",w.input_sum,w.output_sum,w.white,w.updates,w.discarded_slots,w.boundary_loss,w.balance_residual);
  const auto stencil=dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_stencil(2,2,0,0);const auto&first=t.steps[0];
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(58,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=3.8;style.height=2.5;style.font_size=22;
  d.node("pixel",{0,0},std::format("Working {}\nOutput {}\nError {}",first.value_before,first.quantized,first.error),style);
  const std::vector<std::string> names{"Right","Down-left","Down","Down-right"};const std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> positions{{5.4,0},{-5.4,-4},{0,-4},{5.4,-4}};
  for(const auto&n:stencil.candidates){std::string text;
    if(n.in_bounds){const auto it=std::find_if(t.updates.begin()+first.update_begin,t.updates.begin()+first.update_end,[&](const auto&u){return u.direction==n.direction;});text=std::format("{}\nTransfer {}\n{} → {}",names[n.direction],it->transfer,it->value_before,it->value_after);}
    else text=std::format("{} outside\nDiscarded share\n{}",names[n.direction],first.boundary_loss);
    const auto id=std::to_string(n.direction);d.node(id,positions[n.direction],text,style).edge("pixel",id,std::format("{}/16",n.numerator));
  }
  d.text({0,2.4},"First actual raster step: no edge renormalization",25).save_svg("build/floyd_steinberg_tiny.svg");
  if(w.white!=2||w.boundary_loss!=2||w.balance_residual!=0)throw std::runtime_error("tiny signed balance");
}
```
