// result_end
\caption(The first error is negative. Three valid transfers update future cells and one outside share is discarded. Across all four steps, input512 minus output510 equals signed boundary loss2.)
\alttext(A native stencil diagram shows working128 quantized255 with error minus127, right transfer minus55.5625, down transfer minus39.6875, down-right minus7.9375, and the outside down-left share minus23.8125.)

The output is [255,0;0,255], with two white cells. Each pixel is quantized once,
but future working cells may receive several additions. The trace stores only actual
in-bounds updates, with their destination value before addition, the double transfer,
and the value after addition. It records the executing kernel without a second run.

> Preserve the original gradient and its three bands

The native fixture uses the original formula255×column/63 on every one of40 rows.
Its64 columns are split at21 and42, exactly as in the original program; the final
band is one column wider. The table distinguishes the intended mean from white
fraction and the resulting mean255×fraction. All original white fractions remain
unchanged when rounded to six decimals.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_steinberg_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/grayscale_images.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto input=dm::algorithms::dither_gradient(40,64);const auto result=dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_work(input);
  std::print("| columns | pixels | white pixels | white fraction | input mean | output mean | output minus input |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(auto[begin,end]:std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>>{{0,21},{21,42},{42,64}}){const auto v=dm::algorithms::dither_region_stats(input,result.output,begin,end);std::print("| [{},{}) | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",begin,end,v.pixels,v.white,v.white_fraction,v.input_mean,v.output_mean,v.mean_error);}
  const auto&w=result.work;std::print("\nOriginal gradient: pixels {}; white {}; actual updates {}; direction slots {}; signed boundary loss {:.9f}; balance residual {:.3e}.\n",w.pixels,w.white,w.updates,w.neighbor_slots,w.boundary_loss,w.balance_residual);
  std::vector<std::vector<double>> shown;for(const auto&row:result.output)shown.emplace_back(row.begin(),row.end());
  dm::graphics::diagram_grayscale_images({{input,"Original grayscale ramp"},{shown,"Binary error diffusion"}}).save_svg("build/floyd_steinberg_original.svg");
  if(w.white!=1285)throw std::runtime_error("original binary image");
}
