\alttext(Two native grayscale cell panels show a smooth left-to-right dark-to-light ramp and its binary halftone, with white-pixel density increasing toward the right.)

The preserved fractions are0.157143,0.494048 and0.838636 for the original three
bands. Those arithmetic observations explain the increasing dot density; they do not
certify a perceptual quality score or exact equality of each band's mean. Error can
flow from one band to the next, and from the image into discarded outside shares.

The returned image holds int values0or255. It is binary-valued data, not a packed
one-bit bitmap. Its actual storage includes integer cells and row metadata.

> Compare independent thresholding on a uniform patch

On a uniform128 patch, independent thresholding makes every pixel white. Error
diffusion can instead mix black and white pixels so that the arithmetic mean is
closer to the input. Both algorithms below are native functions; the report only
formats their outputs and measurements. This specific control is evidence about
that patch, not a universal ranking across images, devices or viewing conditions.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_steinberg_comparison.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/grayscale_images.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::vector<double>> input(32,std::vector<double>(32,128.));
  const auto plain=dm::algorithms::threshold_dither(input);const auto diffused=dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_dither(input);
  std::print("| method | pixels | white pixels | white fraction | input mean | output mean | signed mean error |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(bool diffuse:{false,true}){const auto&out=diffuse?diffused:plain;const auto v=dm::algorithms::dither_region_stats(input,out,0,32);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",diffuse?"Diffusion":"Threshold",v.pixels,v.white,v.white_fraction,v.input_mean,v.output_mean,v.mean_error);}
  std::vector<std::vector<double>> left,right;for(const auto&row:plain)left.emplace_back(row.begin(),row.end());for(const auto&row:diffused)right.emplace_back(row.begin(),row.end());
  dm::graphics::diagram_grayscale_images({{left,"Threshold at128"},{right,"Raster diffusion"}}).save_svg("build/floyd_steinberg_comparison.svg");
}
```
