\caption(Uniform64 images of seven sizes show actual binary density and signed boundary accounting. Attempted slots equal4N; valid updates omit the image boundary.)
\alttext(Two native plots show measured white fractions against the intended64-over255 density and the actual direction-slot and destination-update counts versus input pixel count.)

For a nonempty R-by-C rectangle, the valid-update count is
R(C-1)+(R-1)C+2(R-1)(C-1). Counting this stencil and validating every row/value
gives O(R+N) work for N pixels. The by-value ordinary API owns a double scratch
image and returns an integer image, requiring O(R+N) storage. The earlier constant
extra-memory claim omitted these images. Only the per-pixel scalar state is constant.

An owned trace additionally retains the input, N steps and at most4N updates. Its
complete admission bound is2R+7N entries: two outer-row arrays, two cell arrays,
one step per pixel and up to four updates per pixel. Temporary scratch, bytes and
peak RAM are not the quota units. The default one-million-entry cap is checked
before copying trace input; zero disables only that optional cap. No partial trace
or sampled/truncated history is returned.

> Domain, geometry and ownership controls

Every row width is validated before scanning source values. Ragged rows reject even
when the first row has width zero. Every source value must be finite; finite values
outside nominal0..255 are accepted without clipping. Actual double transfers and
updated values must stay finite, so an extreme source can fail if it has a valid
neighbor even though an extreme single pixel succeeds. The grayscale renderer has
its own display domain0..255; that does not change the numerical kernel's input rules.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/floyd_steinberg_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/grayscale_images.hpp>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  bool ragged=false,nonfinite=false,quota=false,overflow=false;const auto maximum=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_dither({{128.,128.},{128.}});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){ragged=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_trace({{std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN()}},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){nonfinite=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_trace({{128.,128.},{128.,128.}},31);}catch(const std::length_error&){quota=true;}
  try{dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_dither({{maximum,0.}});}catch(const std::overflow_error&){overflow=true;}
  auto source=std::vector<std::vector<double>>{{128.,128.},{128.,128.}};const auto original=source;const auto trace=dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_trace(source,32);const bool unchanged=source==original;source[0][0]=7;const bool independent=trace.input==original;
  std::print("Checked controls: ragged rejected {}; NaN rejected before quota {}; whole cap31 rejected {}; cap32 steps {}; neighbor arithmetic overflow rejected {}.\n",ragged,nonfinite,quota,trace.steps.size(),overflow);
  std::print("Ownership: source unchanged after call {}; owned input independent after caller edit {}.\n",unchanged,independent);
  std::print("Cutoff127.75 output {}; exact128 output {}; finite maximum single-pixel output {}.\n",dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_dither({{127.75}})[0][0],dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_dither({{128.}})[0][0],dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_dither({{maximum}})[0][0]);
  const auto full=std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max();const auto stencil=dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_stencil(full,full,0,full-1);
  std::print("Virtual size_t-max top-right center: right {}; down-left {}; down {}; down-right {}.\n",stencil.candidates[0].in_bounds,stencil.candidates[1].in_bounds,stencil.candidates[2].in_bounds,stencil.candidates[3].in_bounds);
  const auto one=dm::algorithms::floyd_steinberg_work({{127.5}});std::print("One-pixel tone control: input {}; output {}; discarded {}; residual {}.\n",one.work.input_sum,one.work.output_sum,one.work.boundary_loss,one.work.balance_residual);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(60,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=4.2;style.height=2.8;style.font_size=23;
  d.node("quota",{0,0},std::format("Whole trace bound32\nCap31 rejects: {}\nCap32 records {} steps",quota,trace.steps.size()),style)
   .node("finite",{6,0},std::format("Finite source required\nNaN rejects: {}\nUpdate overflow: {}",nonfinite,overflow),style)
   .node("owned",{12,0},std::format("Owned result\nCaller unchanged: {}\nIndependent input: {}",unchanged,independent),style)
   .text({6,-3.1},"Validation, complete admission and actual arithmetic are separate checks",24).save_svg("build/floyd_steinberg_controls.svg");
  if(!ragged||!nonfinite||!quota||!overflow||!unchanged||!independent)throw std::runtime_error("checked dithering controls");
}
```
